BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-fine-art-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Fine Art Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:A one-year award enabling an emerging Indian visual artist to p
 ursue independent practice\, with a stipulation to attend a recognised art
  residency programme in India for four weeks during the year. ELIGIBILITY 
 IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens currently living in India\, born on or afte
 r 1 January 1996\, who are either recent graduates\, postgraduates or fina
 l-year students of a leading Indian visual arts institute\, or artists wit
 hout those formal credentials but with a record of exhibition participatio
 n. First-year MA students are not eligible. Awardees submit progress repor
 ts at six months and on completion\, plus documentation of the residency. 
 Applications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. Shortlisti
 ng is expected in late October 2026 with interviews in early November.\n\n
 Organisation: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to India
 n citizens currently living in India.\nAward: INR 300\,000 (around USD 3\,
 400 / EUR 2\,950) for one year\, plus a fully covered four-week art reside
 ncy at an Indian art institution. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve mo
 nths of independent practice\, including a mandatory four-week residency w
 ithin India.\n\nMore: https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e1
 4093-df9b-41c5-af96-ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e14093-df9b-41c5-af96
 -ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens currently living in India.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-theatre-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Theatre Art Award 20
 27
DESCRIPTION:A skill-enhancement award for emerging Indian theatre practitio
 ners\, supporting participation in recognised training workshops\, residen
 cies and similar programmes rather than the production of a specific work.
  ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens born after 1 January 1991\, wi
 th preference given to holders of a theatre degree from a leading Indian i
 nstitution. Recipients report at the six-month mark and on completion. App
 lications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. The foundatio
 n runs several other awards on adjacent deadlines\, including the Inlaks-A
 ttakkalari Dance Studentship (30 August 2026) and a two-month Inlaks Resid
 ency at the International Center of Photography in the USA for emerging In
 dian photographic practitioners (31 August 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Inlaks 
 Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to Indian citizens.\nAward: I
 NR 15\,000 per month for up to 12 months\, around INR 180\,000 total (roug
 hly USD 2\,050 / EUR 1\,780). No application fee.\nDuration: Up to twelve 
 months of skill enhancement\, with six-month interim and final reporting.\
 n\nMore: https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vh-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
SUMMARY:Deadline: VH AWARD 2026 (Hyundai Motor Group)
DESCRIPTION:The VH AWARD\, hosted by Hyundai Motor Group\, supports emergin
 g media artists whose work engages with the context of Asia\, through an o
 nline residency and exhibitions across global platforms. FIELD: audiovisua
 l\, screen-based artworks including video art\, motion graphics\, animatio
 n\, games\, films or newly explored areas\; proposals must suit single-cha
 nnel video presentation (no interactivity). ELIGIBILITY: individuals or co
 llectives whose work engages with the context of Asia\, including artists 
 of Asian descent\, those based in Asia\, and the Asian diaspora. Five fina
 lists are selected\, each receiving a USD 30\,000 production grant and a p
 lace in the Ars Electronica online residency program (masterclasses and 1:
 1 mentoring)\, with networking and exhibition opportunities\; one Grand Pr
 ix recipient (announced 2027) receives an additional USD 30\,000\; a new H
 onorary Mention category recognises one or two further applicants with web
 site features and selected residency components. APPLY: via the VH AWARD w
 ebsite Entry Portal with a video portfolio (max 3 min)\, CV and artist sta
 tement (max 3 pages)\, and a new artwork proposal (max 3 pages) with a ref
 erence video (max 1 min)\; all documents in English\; proposed works must 
 be original and unexhibited. Open call 26 May - 21 July 2026 (KST)\; final
 ists announced September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Hyundai Motor Group\nLocat
 ion: Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with Asi
 a\nAward: Each of five finalists receives a USD 30\,000 production grant p
 lus an Ars Electronica online residency\; the Grand Prix winner receives a
 n additional USD 30\,000 (USD 60\,000 total). Honorary Mentions join selec
 ted residency components. No application fee.\nDuration: Online residency 
 Sep 2026 - Mar 2027 (finalists)\; award ceremony and exhibitions June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral#entry
URL:https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral#entry
LOCATION:Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with 
 Asia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:next-art-ai-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI ART AWARD: NEXT ART AI 2026
DESCRIPTION:NEXT ART AI is an open AI art competition run by the HOBAN Cult
 ural Foundation\, welcoming participants of all backgrounds regardless of 
 career\, nationality or age\, and framed as a way to reflect on the future
  of AI art through new modes of expression and artistic experimentation. T
 WO CATEGORIES: AI IMAGE ART\, for works in a single-image format at 150dpi
  or higher\, submitted as JPG\, JPEG\, PNG or BMP up to 10MB\; and AI VIDE
 O ART\, open to a wide range of video formats including animation\, motion
  graphics and live-action footage enhanced or transformed using AI\, at 10
 80p or higher\, under one minute\, 30 or 60fps recommended\, stereo 48kHz 
 audio recommended\, as mp4 (h.264) or mov. Video entries are submitted as 
 a URL via YouTube\, Vimeo\, Dropbox or OneDrive\, or an alternative platfo
 rm if those are restricted in your region\; links that are inaccessible du
 e to privacy settings may be excluded from judging. WHO CAN ENTER: individ
 uals or teams of up to three including the representative\, though you may
  not submit both as an individual and as part of a team. Team representati
 ves create the account in their own name and all members submit a consent 
 form for personal data. Applicants under 19 need a guardian's signed conse
 nt. One work may be submitted per category. RULES ON AI AND ASSETS: work m
 ust be original and created by the applicant or team\, and must be image o
 r video art created using generative AI platforms. Works that have previou
 sly won an award in another competition are not eligible. Free or paid ext
 ernal assets\, game engines\, AI frameworks\, open-source tools and editin
 g software may be used freely\, but applicants must hold licences permitti
 ng commercial use for every element\, and work infringing third-party righ
 ts is excluded. Even where external assets and editing software are used\,
  the creative process must involve AI\, whether AI-assisted direction\, tr
 ansformation\, generation or other AI-based processes\, and the choice of 
 AI tools\, the scope and method of their use\, and the prompts themselves 
 are all weighed in evaluating the creative use of AI. TIMELINE: applicatio
 ns open 1 September 2026 and close 30 September 2026 at 11:59pm KST\, prel
 iminary round early October\, final round late October\, announcement and 
 ceremony early November\, exhibition late November 2026. Organised and hos
 ted by the HOBAN Cultural Foundation\, sponsored by HOBAN Group\, with Seo
 ul Shinmun and EBN as media partners. Details and schedule are subject to 
 change at the organiser's discretion.\n\nOrganisation: HOBAN Cultural Foun
 dation\nLocation: Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibit
 ion in South Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
 \nAward: Total prize pool of KRW 21\,000\,000 across 20 winners\, paid aft
 er deduction of applicable taxes and public charges. Grand Prize KRW 5\,00
 0\,000 (selected regardless of category)\; in each of the two categories\,
  First Prize KRW 2\,000\,000\, three Second Prizes of KRW 1\,000\,000 each
 \, and five Honorable Finalist awards of KRW 500\,000 each\; plus a HOBAN 
 Group President's Award of KRW 1\,000\,000. Winners also receive plaques a
 nd certificates\, online and offline exhibition opportunities\, and a feat
 ure on the official online platform. No entry fee is mentioned.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; exhibition late November 2026\n\nMore: https://next
 -art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://next-art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibition in Sou
 th Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
